{
  "title": "Ziyarat-e-Imam Husain (a.s.) on the Day of Arafah",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "The method of visiting Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)’s tomb on the ‘Arafat Day, according to the words of master scholars and chiefs of our sect and faith, is as follows:\nIf you intend to visit Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) (on the ‘Arafat Day), you may bathe yourself using water from the River Euphrates if possible and any other possibly obtained water. You may then put on the purest (and cleanest) of your clothes and walk towards the holy shrine with tranquility and solemnity. When you reach the gate of the holy shrine (i.e. Ha’ir), you may profess Almighty Allah’s most greatness:\nاَللهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHO AKBAR\nAllah is the Most Great.\nThen, say the following words:\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ كَبِيْرًا وَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ كَثِيْرًا \nALLAAHO AKBARO KABEERAN WAL-HAMDO LILLAAHE KASEERAN \nAllah is the Most Great of all. All praise be to Allah very much. \nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ بُكْرَةً وَ اَصِيْلًا \nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE BUKRATAWN WA ASEELAN \nGlory be to Allah in mornings and evenings. \nوَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ هَدَانَا لِهٰذَا \nWALHAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE HADAANAA LE-HAAZAA \nAll praise be to Allah Who has guided us to this. \nوَ مَا كُنَّا لِنَهْتَدِيَ لَوْ لَاۤ اَنْ هَدَانَا اللّٰهُ \nWA KUNNA LE-NAHTADEYA LAWLAA AN HADAANAL LAAHO \nWe would not have been guided if Allah had not guided us. \nلَقَدْ جَاۤءَتْ رُسُلُ رَبِّنَا بِالْحَقِّ \nLAQAD JAA-AT ROSOLO RABBENAA BIL-HAQQE\nThe messengers of our Lord have indeed come with the truth. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ \nASSALAAMO A’LAA RASOOLIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon the Messenger of Allah, peace of Allah be upon him and his Household. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAA AMEERIL MOMENEENA \nPeace be upon the Commander of the Faithful. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاۤءِ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَاۤءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAA FAATEMATAZ ZAHRAAA-E SAYYEDATE NESAAA-IL A’ALAMEENA \nPeace be upon Fatimah the luminous and the doyenne of all women of the world. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْحَسَنِ وَ الْحُسَيْنِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAL HASANE WAL-HUSAYNE \nPeace be upon al-Hasan and al-Husayn. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAA A’LIYYIB NIL HUSAYNE \nPeace be upon 'Ali the son of al-Husayn. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ \nASSALAAMO A’LAA MOHAMMAD IBNE A’LIYYIN \nPeace be upon Muhammad the son of 'Ali \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى جَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nASSALAAMO A’LAA JA’FAR IBNE MOHAMMADIN \nPeace be upon Ja'far the son of Muhammad. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُوْسَى بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ \nASSALAAMO A’LAA MOOSAB NE JA’FARIN\nPeace be upon Musa the son of Ja'far. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُوْسٰى \nASSALAAMO A’LAA A’LIYY IBNE MOOSAA\nPeace be upon ‘Ali the son of Musa. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ \nASSALAAMO A’LAA MOHAMMAD IBNE A’LIYYIN \nPeace be upon Muhammad the son of 'Ali. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nASSALAAMO A’LAA ALIYY IBNE MOHAMMADIN \nPeace be upon 'Ali the son of Muhammad. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ \nASSALAAMO A’LAL HASAN IBNE A’LIYYIN \nPeace be upon al-Hasan the son of 'Ali. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْخَلَفِ الصَّالِحِ الْمُنْتَظَرِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAL KHALAFIS SAALEHIL MUNTAZARE \nPeace be upon the virtuous Successor and Awaited. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَبَا عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O Abu-'Abdullah. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA RASOOLIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O son of Allah’s Messenger. \nعَبْدُكَ وَ ابْنُ عَبْدِكَ وَ ابْنُ اَمَتِكَ \nA’BDOKA WABNO A’BDEKA WABNO AMATEKAL \nI—the servant of you and the son of your servant and your bondwoman, \nالْمُوَالِيْ لِوَلِيِّكَ الْمُعَادِيْ لِعَدُوِّكَ \nMOWAALEE LE-WALIYYEKAL MO-A’ADEE LE-A’DUWWEKAS \nwho is loyal to those who are loyal to you and enemy of those who are your enemies— \nاسْتَجَارَ بِمَشْهَدِكَ وَ تَقَرَّبَ اِلَى اللّٰهِ بِقَصْدِكَ \nTAJAARA BE-MASH-HADEKA WA TAQARRABA ELAL LAAHE BE-QASDEKA \nam seeking the shelter of your shrine and seeking nearness to Allah through directing to you. \nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ هَدَانِيْ لِوِلَايَتِكَ \nAL-HAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE HADAANEE LE-WELAAYATEKA \nAll praise be to Allah Who guided me to be loyal to you, \nوَ خَصَّنِيْ بِزِيَارَتِكَ وَ سَهَّلَ لِيْ قَصْدَكَ.\nWA KHASSANEE BE-ZEYAARATEKA WA SAH-HALA LEE QASDAKA.\nWho conferred upon me with my visiting you, and Who made easy for me to direct to you.\n`You may then enter the shrine, stop next to the side of the Imam’s head, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اٰدَمَ صِفْوَةِ اللهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA AADAMA SIFWATIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Adam the chosen by Allah. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ نُوْحٍ نَبِىِّ اللهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA NOOHIN NABIYYIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Nooh the prophet of Allah. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِ اللهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Ibrahim the friend of Allah. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُوْسىٰ كَلِيْمِ اللهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA MOOSAA KALEEMIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Moosa the spoken by Allah. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عِيْسٰى رُوْحِ اللهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA E’ESAA ROOHIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Isa the spirit of Allah. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُحَمَّدٍ حَبِيْبِ اللهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA MOHAMMADIN HABEEBIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Muhammad the most beloved by Allah. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA AMEERIL MOMENEENA \nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of the Commander of the Faithful (a.s.). \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَآءِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA FAATEMATAZ ZAHRAAA-E \nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Fatemah (s.a.) the luminous. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ مُحَمَّدٍ ۨ الْمُصْطَفٰى \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA MOHAMMADENIL MUSTAFAA \nPeace be upon you, O son of Muhammad (s.a.w.a.) the well-chosen prophet. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ عَلِىٍّ ۨ الْمُرْتَضٰى \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA A’LIYYENIL MURTAZAA \nPeace be upon you, O son of Ali (a.s.) the well-pleased. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَآءِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA FAATEMATAZ ZAHRAAA-E \nPeace be upon you, O son of Fatemah (s.a.) the luminous. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ خَدِيْجَةَ الْكُبْرٰى \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA KHADEEJATAL KUBRAA \nPeace be upon you, O son of Khadijah (s.a.) the grand lady. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ثَارَ اللهِ وَ بْنَ ثَارِهٖ وَ الْوِتْرَ الْمَوْتُوْرَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA SAARAL LAAHE WABNA SAAREHI WAL WITRAL MAWTOORA \nPeace be upon you, O vengeance of Allah and son of His vengeance and the unavenged sanctity.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلٰوةَ \nASH-HADO ANNAKA QAD AQAMTAS SALAATA \nI bear witness that you performed the prayers, \nوَ اٰتَيْتَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَ اَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ \nWA AATAYTAZ ZAKAATA WA AMARTA BIL MA’ROOFE \ndefrayed the poor-rates, enjoined the right, \nوَ نَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَ اَطَعْتَ اللهَ حَتّٰى اَتٰكَ الْيَقِيْنُ \nWA NAHAYTA A’NIL MUNKARE WA A-TA’TAL LAAHA HATTAA ATAAKAL YAQEENO \nforbade the wrong and obeyed Allah until death came upon you. \nفَلَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً قَتَلَتْكَ وَ لَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً ظَلَمَتْكَ \nFA-LA’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN QATALATKA WA LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN ZALAMATKA \nMay Allah curse the people who slew you. May Allah curse the people who wronged you. \nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً سَمِعَتْ بِذٰلِكَ فَرَضِيَتْ بِهٖ \nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN SAME-A’T BE-ZAALEKA FARAZEYAT BEHI \nMay Allah curse the people who were informed about that but they approved it. \nيَا مَوْلَاىَ يَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ اُشْهِدُ اللهَ وَ مَلَآئِكَتَهٗ \nYAA MAWLAAYA YAA ABA A’BDILLAAHE USH-HEDUL LAAHA WA MALAAA-EKATAHU \nO my master! O Abu Abdillah! I call Allah, His angels, \nوَ اَنْبِيَآئَهٗ وَ رُسُلَهٗ اَنِّىْ بِكُمْ مُّؤْمِنٌ \nWA AMBEYAAA-AHU WA ROSOLAHU ANNEE BEKUM MOMENUN \nHis Prophets and His Messengers to witness that I believe in you \nوَ بِاِيَابِكُمْ مُّوْقِنٌ بِشَرَايِعِ دِيْنِىْ \nWA BE-EYAABEKUM MOOQENUN BE-SHARAA-YE-E’ DEENEE \nand in your return and I have faith in the laws of my religion \nوَ خَوَاتِيْمِ عَمَلِىْ وَ مُنْقَلَبِىْ اِلٰى رَبِّىْ \nWA KHAWAATEEME A’MALEE WA MUNQALABEE ELAA RABBEE \nand in the sealing deeds of mine and in my final return to my Lord. \nفَصَلَوَاتُ اللهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَ عَلٰى اَرْوَاحِكُمْ \nFA-SALAWAATUL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA A’LAA ARWAAHEKUM \nAllah’s blessings be upon you all, upon your souls, \nوَ عَلٰى اَجْسَادِكُمْ وَ عَلٰى شَاهِدِكُمْ \nWA A’LAA AJSAADEKUM WA A’LAA SHA-HEDEKUM \nupon your bodies, upon the present \nوَ عَلٰى غَآئِبِكُمْ وَ ظَاهِرِكُمْ وَ بَاطِنِكُمْ \nWA A’LAA GHAAA-EBEKUM WA ZAAHEREKUM WA BAATENEKUM \nand the absent (of your group) and upon the manifest and the hidden (of your affairs). \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA KHAATAMIN NABIYYEENA \nPeace be upon you, O son of the Seal of Prophets, \nوَ بْنَ سَيِّدِ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ وَ بْنَ اِمَامِ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ \nWAB NA SAYYEDIL WASIYYEENA WAB NA EMAAMIL MUTTAQEENA \nson of the chief of the Prophets’ successors, son of the leader of the pious \nوَ بْنَ قَآئِدِ الْغُرِّ الْمُحَجَّلِيْنَ اِلٰى جَنَّاتِ النَّعِيْمِ \nWAB NA QAAA-EDIL GHURRIL MOHAJJALEENA ELAA JANNAATIN NA-E’EME \nand son of the white-forehead, white-marked ones, (guiding them) to the Gardens of Bliss.\nوَ كَيْفَ لَا تَكُوْنُ كَذٰلِكَ وَ اَنْتَ بَابُ الْهُدٰى \nWA KAYKA LAA TAKOONO KAZAALEKA WA ANTA BAABUL HODAA \nHow can that you be anything other than this while you are the door to the true guidance, \nوَ اِمَامُ التُّقٰى وَ الْعُرْوَةُ الْوُثْقٰى \nWA EMAAMUT TOQAA WAL-U’RWATUL WUSQAA \nthe guide to piety, the firmest handle, \nوَ الْـحُجَّةُ عَلٰى اَهْلِ الدُّنْيَا وَ خَامِسُ اَصْحَابِ الْكِسَآءِ \nWAL-HUJJATO A’LAA AHLID DUNYAA WA KHAAMESO AHLE ASHAABIL KESAAA-E \nthe argument against the inhabitants of this world and the fifth of the People of the Cloak. \nغَذَتْكَ يَدُ الرَّحْمَةِ وَ رَضَعْتَ مِنْ ثَدْىِ الْاِيْمَانِ \nGHA-ZATKA YADUR RAHMATE WA RAZA’TA MIN SAD-YIL EEMAANE \nYou were nourished by the hand of mercy, breast-fed by the bosom of faith \nوَ رُبِّيْتَ فِىْ حِجْرِ الْاِسْلَامِ \nWA RUBBEETA FEE HIJRIL ISLAAME \nand brought up in the lap of Islam. \nفَالنَّفْسُ غَيْرُ رَاضِيَةٍ بِفِرَاقِكَ وَ لَا شَآكَّةٍ فِىْ حَيٰوتِكَ \nFAN-NAFSO GHAYRO RAAZEYATIN BE-FERAAQEKA WA LAA SHAAAK-KATIN FEE HAYAATEKA \nSo, my soul is definitely displeased by the way you left this world and it has no doubt that you are alive. \nصَلَوَاتُ اللهِ عَلَيْكَ وَ عَلٰى اٰبَآئِكَ وَ اَبْنَائِكَ \nSALAWAATUL LAAHE A’LAYKA WA A’LAA AABAAA-EKA WA ABNAA-EKA\nAllah’s blessings be upon you, your ascendants and your descendants. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَرِيْعَ الْعَبْرَةِ السَّاكِبَةِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA SAREE-A’L A’BRATIS SAAKEBATE \nPeace be upon you, O object of the pouring tears \nوَ قَرِيْنَ الْمُصِيْبَةِ الرَّاتِبَةِ \nWA QAREENAL MOSEEBATIR RAATEBATE \nand match of the astounding misfortune. \nلَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً اسْتَحَلَّتْ مِنْكَ الْمَحَارِمَ \nLA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN NIS-TAHALLAT MINKAL MA-HAAREMA \nMay Allah curse the people who violated your sanctities and infringed the holiness of Islam. \nفَقُتِلْتَ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْكَ مَقْهُوْرًا \nFA-QOTILTA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYKA MAQHOORAN \nSo, you – may Allah’s blessings be upon you – were killed overwhelmed, \nوَ اَصْبَحَ رَسُوْلُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ بِكَ مَوْتُوْرًا \nWA ASHBA-HA RASOOLUL LAAHE SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI BEKA MAWTOORAN \nthe Messenger of Allah, Allah’s blessings be upon him and his Household, became cut off \nوَ اَصْبَحَ كِتَابُ اللهِ بِفَقْدِكَ مَهْجُوْرًا \nWA ASBAHA KETAABUL LAAHE BE-FAQDEKA MAHJOORAN \nbecause of loss of you and the Book of Allah became deserted due to losing you. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَ عَلٰى جَدِّكَ وَ اَبِيْكَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA WA A’LAA JADDEKA WA ABEEKA \nPeace be upon you, your grandfather, your father, \nوَ اُمِّكَ وَ اَخِيْكَ وَ عَلَى الْاَئِمَّةِ مِنْ بَۢنِيْكَ \nWA UMMEKA WA AKHEEKA WA A’LAL A-IMMATE MIM BANEEKA \nyour mother, your brother, the Imams from your descendants, \nوَ عَلَى الْمُسْتَشْهَدِيْنَ مَعَكَ \nWA A’LAL MUSTASH-HADEENA MA-A’KA \nthose who were martyred with you \nوَ عَلَى الْمَلَآئِكَةِ الْـحَآفِّيْنَ بِقَبْرِكَ \nWA A’LAL MALAAA-EKATIL HAAAF-FEENA BE-QABREKA \nand the angels who are surrounding your tomb, \nوَ الشَّاهِدِيْنَ لِزُوَّارِكَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nWASH SHAAHEDEENA LE-ZUWWAAREKAL MOMENEENA \nwitnessing for your visitors and praying \nبِالْقَبُوْلِ عَلٰى دُعَآءِ شِيْعَتِكَ \nBIL-QABOOLE A’LAA DO-AAA-E SHEE-A’TEKA \nfor the acceptance of the prayers of your adherents. \nوَ السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَ رَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَ بَرَكَاتُهٗ. \nWAS SALAAMO A’LAYKA WA RAHMATUL LAAHE WA BARAKAATOHU \nPeace and Allah’s mercy and blessings be upon you. \nبِاَبِىْ اَنْتَ وَ اُمِّىْ يَا بْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللهِ \nBE-ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE YABNA RASOOLIL LAAHE \nMay my father and mother be ransoms for you, O son of Allah’s Messenger. \nبِاَبِىْ اَنْتَ وَ اُمِّىْ يَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ \nBE-ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE YAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE \nMay my father and mother be ransoms for you, O Abu-Abdillah. \nلَقَدْ عَظُمَتِ الرَّزِيَّةُ وَ جَلَّتِ الْمُصِيْبَةُ بِكَ عَلَيْنَا \nLAQAD A’ZOMATIR RAZIYYATO WA JALLATIL MOSEEBATO BEKA A’LAYNAA \nSo unbearable is the misfortune and so horrendous is the calamity of you for us \nوَ عَلٰى جَمِيْعِ اَهْلِ السَّمٰوَاتِ وَ الْاَرْضِ \nWA A’LAA JAMEE-E’ AHLIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE \nand for all the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth. \nفَلَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً اَسْرَجَتْ وَ اَلْـجَمَتْ \nFA-LA’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN ASRAJAT WA ALJAMAT \nMay Allah curse the people who put saddles and reins on their animals \nوَ تَهَيَّاَتْ لِقِتَالِكَ يَا مَوْلَاىَ يَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اللهِ \nWA TAHAYYA-AT LE-QETAALEKA YAA MAWLAAYA YAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE \nand readied themselves for fighting against you. O my master! O Abu-Abdillah! \nقَصَدْتُ حَرَمَكَ وَ اَتَيْتُ مَشْهَدَكَ \nQASADTO HARAMAKA WA ATAYTO MASH-HADAKA \nI have directed to your sanctuary and I have come to your shrine \nاَسْئَلُ اللهَ بِالشَّاْنِ الَّذِىْ لَكَ عِنْدَهٗ \nAS-ALUL LAAHA BISH-SHAANIL LAZEE LAKA I’NDAHU \nasking Almighty Allah in the name of the standing that you enjoy with Him \nوَ بِالْمَحَلِّ الَّذِىْ لَكَ لَدَيْهِ \nBIL-MAHALLIL LAZEE LAKA LADAYHE \nand in the name of the position that you occupy with him \nاَنْ يُّصَلِّىَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nAN-Y YOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nto send blessings upon Muhammad (s.a.w.a.) and the Household of Muhammad (a.s.) \nوَ اَنْ يَّجْعَلَنِىْ مَعَكُمْ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَ الْاٰخِرَةِ \nWA AN-Y YAJ-A’LANEE MA-A’KUM FID-DUNYAA WAL AAKHERATE \nand to include me with your group in this world and in the Hereafter, \nبِمَنِّهٖ وَ جُوْدِهٖ وَ كَرَمِهٖ.\nBE-MANNEHI WA JOODEHI WA KARAMEHI.\nout of His favor, magnanimity and generosity.\nYou may then kiss the tomb and offer a two-unit prayer in which you may recite any Surah you wish. Upon accomplishment, you may say the following supplicatory words:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ صَلَّيْتُ وَ رَكَعْتُ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE SALLAYTO WA RA-KA’TO \nO Allah, I have offered a prayer, genuflected \nوَ سَجَدْتُ لَكَ وَحْدَكَ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَكَ \nWA SAJADTO LAKA WAHDAKA LAA SHAREEKA LAKA \nand prostrated myself for Your sake purely without setting any partner with You, \nلِاَنَّ الصَّلَاةَ وَ الرُّكُوْعَ وَ السُّجُوْدَ \nLE-ANNAS SALAATA WAR-ROKOO-A’ WAS SOJOODA \nsince all prayers, genuflections and prostrations \nلَا تَكُوْنُ اِلَّا لَكَ لِاَنَّكَ اَنْتَ اللهُ \nLAA TAKOONO ILLAA LAKA LE-ANNAKA ANTAL LAAHO \nsuit none except You. Because You are Allah; \nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA \nthere in no god save You. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nO Allah, (please) send blessings upon Muhammad (s.a.w.a.) and the Household of Muhammad (a.s.), \nوَ اَبْلِغْهُمْ عَنِّىْ اَفْضَلَ الْتَّحِيَّةِ وَ السَّلَامِ \nWA ABLIGH-HUM A’NNEE AFZALAT TAHIYYATE WAS SALAAME \nconvey to them my best greetings and compliments \nوَارْدُدْ عَلَىَّ مِنْهُمُ التَّحِيَّةَ وَ السَّلَامَ \nWAR DUD A’LAYYA MINHOMUT TAHIYYATA WAS SALAAMA A\nand convey to me their replies to my greetings and compliments. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ هَاتَانِ الرَّكْعَتَانِ هَدِيَّةٌ مِّنِّىْ \nLLAAHUMMA WA HAATAANIR RAK-A’TAANE HADIYYATUM MINNEE \nO Allah, these two units of prayer are present from me \nاِلٰى مَوْلَاىَ وَ سَيِّدِىْ وَ اِمَامِىْ \nELAA MAWLAAYA WA SAYYEDEE WA EMAAMEE \nto my master, chief and leader, \nحُسَيْنِ بْنِ عَلِىٍّ عَلَيْهِمَا السَّلَامُ \nHUSAYN IBNE A’LIYYIN A’LAYHEMAS SALAAMO \nHusain the son of Ali, peace be upon both of them. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADINW \nO Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad (s.a.w.a.) and the Household of Muhammad (a.s.) \nوَّ تَقَبَّلْ ذٰلِكَ مِنِّىْ وَ اجْزِنِىْ عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ \nWA TAQABBAL ZAALEKA MINNEE WAJ ZENEE A’LAA ZAALEKA \nand accept that from me and reward me for it \nاَفْضَلَ اَمَلِىْ وَ رَجَآئِىْ فِيْكَ وَ فِىْ وَلِيِّكَ \nAFZALA AMALEE WA RAJAAA-EE FEEKA WA FEE WALIYYEKA \nin the best rewarding that I anticipate and hope from You and from Your saint. \nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ.\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEEN.\nO most merciful of all those who show mercy! \nYou may then turn to the side of the Imam’s feet and visit Ali ibn al-Husayn (a.s.) whose head is at the side of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)’s feet, and say these words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAB NA RASOOLIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O son of Allah’s Messenger. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ نَبِىِّ اللهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAB NA NABIYYIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O son of Allah’s Prophet. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA AMEERIL MOMENEENA \nPeace be upon you, O son of the Commander of the Faithful. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ الْحُسِيْنِ الشَّهِيْدِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAB NAL HUSAYNISH SHAHEEDE \nPeace be upon you, O son of al-Husain (a.s.) the martyr. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الشَّهِيْدُ ابْنُ الشَّهِيْدِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA AYYOHASH SHAHEED UBNUSH SHAHEEDE \nPeace be upon you, O martyr and son of the martyr. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْمَظْلُوْمُ ابْنُ الْمَظْلُوْمِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA AYYOHAL MAZLOOM UBNUL MAZLOOME \nPeace be upon you, O persecuted and son of the persecuted. \nلَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً قَتَلَتْكَ وَ لَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً ظَلَمَتْكَ \nLA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN QATALATKA WA LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN ZALAMATKA \nMay Allah curse the people who slew you. May Allah curse the people who wronged you. \nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً سَمِعَتْ بِذٰلِكَ فَرَضِيَتْ بِهٖ \nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN SAME-A’T BE-ZAALEKA FA-RAZEYAT BEHI \nMay Allah curse the people who were informed of that and they approved it. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْلَاىَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA MAWLAAYA \nPeace be upon you, O my master. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَلِىَّ اللهِ وَ بْنَ وَلِيِّهٖ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WALIYYAL LAAHE WAB NA WALIYYEHI \nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s friend and son of His friend. \nلَقَدْ عَظُمَتِ الْمُصِيْبَةُ \nLAQAD A’ZOMATIL MOSEEBATO \nUnbearable is the misfortune \nوَ جَلَّتِ الرَّزِيَّةُ بِكَ عَلَيْنَا \nWA JALLATIR RAZIYYATO BEKA A’LAYNAA \nand so horrendous is the calamity of you for us \nوَ عَلٰى جَمِيْعِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nWA A’LAA JAMEE-I’L MOMENEENA \nand for all faithful believers. \nفَلَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً قَتَلَتْكَ \nFA-LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN QATALATKA \nMay Allah curse the people who slew you. \nوَ اَبْرَءُ اِلَى اللهِ وَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْهُمْ \nWA ABRA-O ELAL LAAHE WA ELAYKA MINHUM \nI release myself in the presence of Allah and you from these people \nفِى الدُّنْيَا وَ الْاٰخِرَةِ.\nFID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERATE.\nin this world and in the Hereafter.\nYou may then turn your face to the martyrs and visit them with the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا اَوْلِيَآءَ اللهِ وَ اَحِبَّآئَهٗ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM YAA AWLEYAAA-AL LAAHE WA AHIBBAAA-AHU\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s friends and beloved by him. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا اَصْفِيَآءَ اللهِ وَ اَوِدَّآئَهٗ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM YAA ASFEYAAA ALLAAHE WA AWIDDAAA-AHU \nPeace be upon you, O choices of Allah and His favorites. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا اَنْصَارَ دِيْنِ اللهِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM YAA ANSAARA DEENIL LAAHE \nPeace be upon you, O supporters of Allah’s Religion, \nوَ اَنْصَارَ نَبِيِّهٖ وَ اَنْصَارَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nWA ANSAARA NABIYYEHI WA ANSAARA AMEERIL MOMENEENA \nsupporters of His Prophet, supporters of the Commander of the Faithful \nوَ اَنْصَارَ فَاطِمَةَ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَآءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ \nWA ANSAARA FAATEMATA SAYYEDATE NESAAA-IL A’ALAMEENA \nand supporters of Fatemah the doyenne of the women of the world. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا اَنْصَارَ اَبِىْ مُحَمَّدٍۨ الْـحَسَنِ الْوَلِىِّ النَّاصِحِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM YAA ANSAARA ABEE MOHAMMADENIL HASANIL WALIYYIN NAASEHE \nPeace be upon you, O supporters of Abu-Muhammad al-Hasan the sincere saint. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَا اَنْصَارَ اَبِىْ عَبْدِ اللهِ الْحُسَيْنِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM YAA ANSAARA ABEE A’BDIL LAAHIL HUSAYNISH \nPeace be upon you, O supporters of Abu-Abdullah al-Husain \nالشَّهِيْدِ الْمَظْلُوْمِ صَلَوَاتُ اللهِ عَلَيْهِمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ \nSHAHEEDIL MAZLOOME SALAWAATUL LAAHE A’LAYHIM AJMA-E’ENA \nthe wronged martyr. Blessings of Allah be upon them all. \nبِاَبِىْ اَنْتُمْ وَ اُمِّىْ طِبْتُمْ وَ طَابَتِ الْاَرْضُ الَّتِىْ فِيْهَا دُفِنْتُمْ \nBE-ABEE ANTUM WA UMMEE TIBTUM WA TAABATIL ARZUL LATEE FEEHAA DOFINTUM \nMay my father and mother be your ransoms. Pure are you and pure is the soil in which you were buried. \nوَ فُزْتُمْ وَ اللهِ فَوْزًا عَظِيْمًا يَا لَيْتَنِىْ كُنْتُ مَعَكُمْ \nWA FUZTUM WAL LAAHE FAWZAN A’ZEEMAN YAA LAYTANEE KUNTO MA-A’KUM \nAnd, by Allah, great is your triumph. I wish I were with you \nفَاَفُوْزَ مَعَكُمْ فِىْ الْجِنَانِ مَعَ الشُّهَدَآءِ وَ الصَّالِحِيْنَ \nFA-A-FOOZA MA-A’KUM FIL JENAANE MA-A’SH SHOHA-DAAA-E WAS-SAALEHEENA \nso that I would have won with you in the gardens of Paradise with the martyrs and the righteous. \nوَ حَسُنَ اُوْلٰٓئِكَ رَفِيْقًا وَ السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَ رَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَ بَرَكَاتُهٗ.\nWA HASONA OOLAAA-EKA RAFEEQAN WAS SALAAMO A’LAYKUM WA RAHMATUL LAAHE WA BARAKAATOHU.\nExcellent is the companionship of these. Peace and Allah’s mercy and blessings be upon you all.\nYou may then return to the side of Imam al-Husayn’s head and pray as frequently as possible for yourself, your family members, and your brethren-in-faith.\nSayyid Ibn Tawus and al-Shahid added the following:\nYou may then walk to the shrine of al-’Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. When you reach there, you may stop at the tomb and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اَبَا الْفَضْلِ الْعَبَّاسَ بْنَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA ABAL FAZLIL A’BBAAS ABNA AMEERIL MOMENEENA\nPeace be upon you, O Abul Fazl al-Abbas son of the Commander of the Faithful. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ سَيِّدِ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA SAYYEDIL WASIYYEENA \nPeace be upon you, O son of the chief of the Prophets’ successors. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بْنَ اَوَّلِ الْقَوْمِ اِسْلَامًا \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA AWWALIL QAWME ISLAAMAN \nPeace be upon you, O son of the foremost in accepting Islam, \nوَ اَقْدَمِهِمْ اِيْمَانًا وَ اَقْوَمِهِمْ بِدِيْنِ اللهِ \nWA AQDAMEHIM EEMAANAN WA AQWAMEHIM BE-DEENIL LAAHE \nthe leading in having faith in it, the most perfect in carrying out the laws of Allah’s religion \nوَ اَحْوَطِهِمْ عَلَى الْاِسْلَامِ \nWA AHWATEHIM A’LAL ISLAAME \nand the most careful for Islam. \nاَشْهَدُ لَقَدْ نَصَحْتَ لِلّٰهِ وَ لِرَسُوْلِهٖ وَ لِاَخِيْكَ فَنِعْمَ الْاَخُ الْمُوَاسِىْ \nASH-HADO LAQAD NASAH-TA LILLAAHE WA LE-RASOOLEHI WA LE-AKHEEKA FA-NE’MAL AKHUL MOWAASEE \nI bear witness that you have acted sincerely for the sake of Allah, His Messenger and your brother. So, how excellent sacrificing brother you are! \nفَلَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً قَتَلَتْكَ وَ لَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً ظَلَمَتْكَ \nFA-LA-A’-NAL LAAHO UMMATAN QATALATKA WA LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATAN ZALAMATKA \nMay Allah curse the people who slew you. May Allah curse the people who wronged you. \nوَ لَعَنَ اللهُ اُمَّةً اِسْتَحَلَّتْ مِنْكَ الْمَحَارِمَ \nWA LA-A’NAL LAAHO UMMATANIS TAHALLAT MINKAL MAHAAREMA \nMay Allah curse the people who violated your sanctities \nوَ انْتَهَكَتْ فِىْ قَتْلِكَ حُرْمَةَ الْاِسْلَامِ \nWAN TAHAKAT FEE QATLEKA HURMATAL ISLAAME \nand infringed the holiness of Islam when they killed you. \nفَنِعْمَ الْاَخُ الصَّابِرُ الْمُجَاهِدُ الْمُحَامِى النَّاصِرُ \nFA-NE’MAL AKHUS SAABERUL MOJAAHEDUL MOHAAMIN NAASERO \nMost excellent steadfast, striver brother, defender, supporter, \nوَ الْاَخُ الدَّافِعُ عَنْ اَخِيْهِ الْمُجِيْبُ اِلٰى طَاعَةِ رَبِّهِ \nWAL AKHUD DAA-FE-O’ A’N AKHEEHIL MOJEEBO ELAA TAA-A’TE RABBEHIR \none who stood up for his brother, one who responded to the obedience to his Lord \nالرَّاغِبُ فِيْمَا زَهِدَ فِيْهِ غَيْرُهٗ مِنَ الثَّوَابِ الْـجَزِيْلِ \nRAAGHEBO FEEMAA ZAHEDA FEEHE GHAYROHU MENAS SAWAABIL JAZEELE \nand one who desired for what others deemed unworthy; namely, the abundant reward \nوَ الثَّنَآءِ الْـجَمِيْلِ وَ اَلْحَقَكَ اللهُ بِدَرَجَةِ اٰبَآئِكَ \nWAS-SANAAA-IL JAMEELE WA AL-HAQAKAL LAAHO BE-DARAJATE AABAAA-EKA \nand the excellent praise you are. May Allah attach you to the rank of your ancestors \nفِىْ دَارِ النَّعِيْمِ اِنَّهٗ حَمِيْدٌ مَّجَيْدٌ.\nFEE DAARIN NA-E’EME INNAHU HAMEEDUM MAJEEDUN.\nin the Abode of Bliss, indeed, He is Praiseworthy, Glorious.\nYou may then throw yourself on the tomb and say the following words:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ تَعَرَّضْتُ و لِزِيَارَةِ اَوْلِيَآئِكَ \nALLAAHUMMA LAKA TA-A’RRAZTO WA LE-ZEYAARATE AWLE-YAAA-EKA\n“O Allah! To You I present myself, and for the visitation of Your friends (beloved ones) \nقَصَدْتُ رَغْبَةً فِىْ ثَوَابِكَ وَ رَجَآءً لِمَغْفِرَتِكَ \nQASAD-TO RAGHBATAN FEE SAWAABEKA WA RAJAAA-AN LE-MAGHFERATEKA \nI have set out — seeking Your reward, hoping for Your forgiveness \nوَ جَزِيْلِ اِحْسَانِكَ \nWA JAZEELE EHSAANEKA \nand Your abundant kindness.\nفَاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّىَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nFA-AS-ALOKA AN TOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADINW \nSo I ask You to send blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, \nوَّ اَنْ تَـجْعَلَ رِزْقِى بِهِمْ دَارًّا \nWA AN TAJ-A’LA RIZQEE BEHIM DAARRANW \nand to make my sustenance through them abundant, \nوَّ عَيْشِىْ بِهِمْ قَارًّا وَّ زِيَارَتِىْ بِهِمْ مَقْبُوْلَةً \nWA A’YSHEE BEHIM QAARRANW WA ZEYAARATEE BEHIM MAQBOOLATANW \nmy life through them stable, my visitation through them accepted, \nوَّ ذَنْۢبِىْ بِهِمْ مَغْفُوْرًا وَ اقْلِبْنِىْ بِهِمْ مُفْلِحًا مُنْجِحًا \nWA ZAMBEE BEHIM MAGHFOORATAN WAQ LIBNEE BEHIM MUFLEHAN MUNJEHAN \nand my sins through them forgiven. And turn me back, by their means, successful, \nمُسْتَجَابًا دُعآئِىْ بِاَفْضَلِ مَا يَنْقَلِبُ بِهٖ اَحَدٌ مِّنْ زُوَّارِهٖ \nMUSTAJAABAN DO-A’AA-EE BE-AFZALE MAA YANQALEBO BEHI AHADUM MIN ZUWWAAREHI \nprosperous, and with my supplication answered — with the best outcome that any of their visitors \nوَ الْقَاصِدِيْنَ اِلَيْهِ بِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ.\nWAL QAASEDEENA ELAYHE BE-RAHMATEKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEEN.\nand those who come to them return with — by Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nYou may then kiss the tomb and offer there the prayer of ziyarah as well as any other prayer you wish to offer. When you intend to bid farewell to him, you may say the words that have been previously cited at bidding farewell.",
  "merits": "Be it known to you that the traditions that are reported from the Ahl al-Bayt the Immaculate and infallible about the merits and advantages of visiting Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) on the ‘Arafat Day are innumerable. Heading for filling the dear believers with desire for visiting Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) on this day, we will hereinafter cite a few number of these traditions:\nBashir al-Dahhan, through a valid chain of authority, has reported that he, once, said to Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.), “Some years, I miss the hajj season; therefore, I present myself at the tomb of al-Husayn (a.s.).” The Imam (a.s.) commented, “Well done, Bashir! Any faithful believer who comes to the tomb of (Imam) al-Husayn (a.s.), Allah’s blessings be upon him, with full recognition of his real position on a day other than the feast days, he shall be granted the reward of twenty times of admissible and acceptable hajj and twenty times of admissible and acceptable ‘umrah as well as the reward of participation in twenty campaigns with a commissioned prophet or a decent leader. Moreover, whoever comes to his (i.e. Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)) tomb on the ‘Arafat Day, with full recognition of his real position, will be granted the reward of one thousand times of admissible and acceptable hajj and one thousand times of admissible and acceptable ‘umrah as well as the reward of participating in one thousand campaigns with a commissioned prophet or a decent leader.”\nBashir said, “What shall I be awarded if I present myself at Mount ‘Arafat on that day?”\nSomewhat angrily, the Imam (a.s.) looked at him and said, “Bashir, if a faithful believer comes to the tomb of (Imam) al-Husayn (a.s.), Allah’s blessings be upon him, on the ‘Arafat Day, washes himself with the water of the River Euphrates, and then turns his face for visiting him, Almighty Allah shall record for him the reward of an entire hajj along with all of its rituals for every step he makes.”\nThe reporter then added, “Most probably, the Imam (a.s.) added to this the reward of an entire ‘umrah (or campaign, according to another form of this report).”\nAccording to many validly reported traditions, on the ‘Arafat Day, Almighty Allah looks at the visitors of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)’s tomb with mercy before He looks at those gathering on ‘Arafat Mountain.\nAccording to another validly reported tradition, Rafa’ah reported that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) once asked him, “Did you go on hajj this year?”\nRafa’ah answered, “May Allah accept me as ransom for you! I did not have enough resources to go to hajj. Rather, I could present myself at the tomb of al-Husayn (a.s.).”\nThe Imam (a.s.) commented, “Rafa’ah, you have thus not failed to gain what those who presented themselves at Mina have gained! Were it not for that I do not want people to desert going on hajj, I would pass on to you a discourse that if you hear it, you will never leave visiting the tomb of al-Husayn, (a.s.) Allah’s blessings be upon you.”\nThe Imam (a.s.) then paused for a while and then continued, “My father has told me that whoever travels to the tomb of al-Husayn (a.s.) recognizing his actual position and showing no pride, will be accompanied by one thousand angels on his right side and one thousand angels on his left. The reward of one thousand times of hajj and one thousand times of ‘umrah with a prophet or a prophet’s successor will also be recorded for him.”"
}
